---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---
<BaseLayout title="Editorial Policy" description="How Mossy Tank researches, writes, and reviews its content.">
  <div class="container prose post">
    <h1>Editorial Policy</h1>
    <p>
      {SITE_TITLE} aims to be the most trustworthy beginner resource for low-tech planted aquariums.
      Here's how we keep our content reliable:
    </p>
    <h2>How we create content</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Hands-on experience first.</strong> Guides reflect real setups and outcomes, not just theory.</li>
      <li><strong>Researched and fact-checked.</strong> We cross-reference reputable hobby sources and manufacturer specs.</li>
      <li><strong>Reviewed before publishing.</strong> Every article is edited by a human for accuracy and clarity.</li>
      <li><strong>Kept current.</strong> We update guides as gear, prices, and best practices change.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      Spotted an error? Email us via the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> and we'll review and
      correct it promptly.
    </p>
    <h2>Animal welfare</h2>
    <p>
      The wellbeing of fish, shrimp, and other livestock always comes first. We will never recommend
      a practice that compromises animal health for aesthetics or convenience.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
